<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal futures mkt studies share derivatives.</title>
<headline>Portugal futures mkt studies share derivatives.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Oporto Derivatives Exchange (BDP) could launch derivative contracts on shares within the year, managing director Manuel Alves Monteiro said.</p>
<p>Alves Monteiro told Reuters that Portugal Telecom and the soon to be partially privatised EDP-Electricidade de Portugal SA were the most likely stocks on which such contracts would be launched.</p>
<p>&quot;This is being studied and we think that it should be possible to start trade this year,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He gave no details on the type of contract being proposed.</p>
<p>--Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
